{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevFupkKAXGSH6pgZGxVA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings (continued):**\n- Error handling pattern at `ShipmentController.kt:29` and `ShipmentController.kt:49` - uses ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException\n- Error codes are defined as enum at `ApiError.kt:31`\n\n**Conventions in this repository:**\n1. Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses, specifically `ConflictException` for HTTP 409 and `ResourceNotFoundException` for HTTP 404\n2. Each error scenario has a machine-readable `ErrorCode` enum value\n3. Tests use MockMvc with `MockMvcRequestBuilders` (get, post)\n4. Tests check status codes with `status()` matchers and response bodies with `jsonPath()`\n5. Tests verify the error envelope structure: `$.error.code` and `$.error.message`\n6. The repository is cleared before each test with `@BeforeEach`\n\n**Affected files and why they cannot be avoided:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` - must add the confirm endpoint\n2. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - must add tests for the new endpoint\n3. `ApiError.kt` - must add error code for shipment state conflict (SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) to distinguish \"cannot confirm a cancelled shipment\" from other errors\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Breaking the error contract if the new error code doesn't match client expectations\n2. Concurrency issues if multiple threads try to confirm the same shipment simultaneously (though ConcurrentHashMap provides atomic operations)\n3. Idempotency requires that confirming an already-confirmed shipment does not fail\n\n**Open questions:** None - the ticket is clear about the four cases and their expected HTTP responses.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** - Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` error code to represent when a shipment cannot be transitioned to CONFIRMED due to its current state (specifically when CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID (throws `ResourceNotFoundException` with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND if missing)\n   - If status is CREATED, transition to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent success)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw `ConflictException` with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n   - Return the (possibly updated) shipment\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add four new test cases:\n   - Confirm a CREATED shipment transitions it to CONFIRMED\n   - Confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without change\n   - Confirm a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with error envelope\n   - Confirm a non-existent shipment returns 404 with error envelope\n\n**Rejected alternatives:**\n- **Add a service layer:** The existing code doesn't have a service layer; all logic is in the controller. Adding one would be unrelated refactoring outside the scope.\n- **Use a different error code for CANCELLED:** Considered reusing SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS but that doesn't semantically fit. SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE is clearer and follows the pattern of having specific codes for each error condition.\n- **Create a separate `ShipmentService` class:** The codebase shows no service layer pattern; controllers directly use repositories. Adding one would change the architecture unnecessarily.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Repository read | Update | Response | HTTP |\n|------|-------|-----------------|--------|----------|------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | shipmentId | findById | save(updated) | Shipment | 200 |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED | shipmentId | findById | none | Shipment | 200 |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | shipmentId | findById | none | ApiError(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) | 409 |\n| Confirm missing | shipmentId | findById returns null | none | ApiError(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) | 404 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: Confirms a created shipment** - Creates shipment, confirms it, verifies status changed to CONFIRMED, persists to repository\n2. **Test: Confirming already-confirmed succeeds** - Creates and confirms shipment, confirms again, verifies no error and status still CONFIRMED\n3. **Test: Confirming cancelled shipment fails** - Writes a CANCELLED shipment directly to repo, attempts confirm, verifies HTTP 409 and error code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n4. **Test: Confirming non-existent shipment fails** - Attempts confirm on non-existent id, verifies HTTP 404 and error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1792,"cache_read_input_tokens":16681,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1792},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"682b858e-36a5-4eaa-b0b4-60f7b8e50fee","uuid":"afffb3a4-47a0-45c3-a175-665959086111","timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:48:13.145Z","request_id":"req_011CevFuomXXGbXvFEgYE7T2"}
