pmentController.kt** - Added 23 lines: the confirm endpoint method that:\n   - Gets shipment by ID (ResourceNotFoundException if missing)\n   - Handles three status cases: CREATED→CONFIRMED transition, CONFIRMED idempotent return, CANCELLED→ConflictException\n   - Returns the shipment\n   - Necessary to implement the BE-003 requirement\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added 67 lines across 4 test methods in a @Nested inner class:\n   - Test confirms CREATED→CONFIRMED with persistence check\n   - Test idempotent confirm on CONFIRMED\n   - Test CANCELLED rejection with 409 and error code\n   - Test missing shipment with 404 and error code\n   - Necessary to verify the new endpoint works per requirements\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are met.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n**Requirement** — Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint that transitions CREATED shipments to CONFIRMED, is idempotent on CONFIRMED, rejects CANCELLED with HTTP 409, and returns HTTP 404 for missing shipments.\n\n**Changed:**\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt` — Added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code for state conflict errors\n- `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` — Added confirm endpoint with state transition logic and error handling\n- `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Added four tests for confirm endpoint covering all four specified cases\n\n**Tests:**\n- `confirms a created shipment and transitions to CONFIRMED` — Verifies CREATED→CONFIRMED transition and persistence\n- `confirming an already-confirmed shipment succeeds and changes nothing` — Verifies idempotent operation on CONFIRMED\n- `confirming a cancelled shipment returns 409 with error envelope` — Verifies HTTP 409 conflict response with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n- `confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with error envelope` — Verifies 